---

<CaseStudy
  title="Brutopia"
  subtitle="A group project. This time, with actual apartments."
  heroPlaceholder="Brutopia hero — garden facade (photo needed)"
  facts={facts}
  gallery={gallery}
  prev={{ href: '/sargfabrik/', label: 'Sargfabrik' }}
  next={{ href: '/bijgaardehof/', label: 'Bijgaardehof' }}
>
  <section class="case-reading mx-auto max-w-[820px] px-6 pt-12 sm:px-12">
    <p>Brutopia in Brussels combines 29 homes with ground-floor workspaces. Its architects, stekke + fraas, identify it as private cohousing: residents collectively shaping a building, rather than a conventional developer choosing the whole program for future buyers. <a class="source-link" href="https://stekkeplusfraas.be/projets/brutopia/">[Project source]</a></p>
    <p>That tells us something useful about the client, but little on its own about who can afford entry, how homes resell, or whether residents have similar incomes. This case is a prompt to investigate the development process; it is not evidence that self-development reliably saves a fixed percentage.</p>
    <h2>Design the decision-making, too.</h2>
    <p>A resident group inherits work that a developer ordinarily coordinates: choices, approvals, risk, contracts and surprises. Some people can contribute lots of time or skilled labor; others cannot. An inclusive process needs paid expertise and ways to participate that do not reward whoever has the most evenings free.</p>
    <p>Before offering unfinished interiors as a budget strategy, compare the full cost of completing an accessible, habitable home. Who handles defects, cost overruns or a household that can no longer finish its part? Saving on the initial contract is not the same as saving overall.</p>
    <aside class="research-note mt-8">Reading lens: project publications document the place and its intended design. They are not independent evaluations of affordability, energy performance or how every resident experiences life there. The questions here are our interpretation.</aside>
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="lessons">
<li>Budget facilitation and project management as real development work.</li>
<li>Make entry requirements, financing and exit rights understandable before recruiting.</li>
<li>Study the workplace-housing mix without assuming commercial demand or subsidy levels transfer.</li>
</Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="sources"><a href="https://stekkeplusfraas.be/projets/brutopia/">stekke + fraas · Brutopia project record</a>. Reviewed October 2026. Approximate counts are identified; population changes over time.</Fragment>
</CaseStudy>
